     "label": "D",
     "text": "14",
     "correct": false
    }
   ],
   "solution": "NaOH is a strong base, so it completely dissociates in water to give OH- ions. The concentration of OH- ions is equal to the concentration of NaOH, which is 0.1 M. Using the equation pOH = -log[OH-], we get pOH = -log(0.1) = 1. Then, pH + pOH = 14, so pH = 14 - pOH = 14 - 1 = 13."
