     "label": "C",
     "text": "2",
     "correct": true
    },
    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "3",
     "correct": false
    }
   ],
   "solution": "To find the maximum or minimum of the function f(x), we need to find the critical points by taking the derivative of f(x) and setting it equal to zero. The derivative of f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 3 is f'(x) = 2x - 4. Setting f'(x) = 0, we get 2x - 4 = 0, which gives x = 2."
  },
